{"name":"Nantucket Dune","hex":"#d0bfaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ridge or hill of sand piled up by currents of wind or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nantucket","blocks":[{"text":"Nantucket is an island in Massachusetts, United States, about 30 miles (48 km) south of the Cape Cod peninsula. Together with the small islands of Tuckernuck and Muskeget, it constitutes the Town and County of Nantucket, a combined county/town government. Nantucket is the southeasternmost town in Massachusetts. The name \"Nantucket\" is adapted from similar Algonquian names for the island."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Nantucket-08-2004.jpg/330px-Nantucket-08-2004.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nantucket","wikidata":"Q49149"},{"title":"Dune","blocks":[{"text":"A dune is a landform composed of wind- or water-driven sand. It typically takes the form of a mound, ridge, or hill. An area with dunes is called a dune system or a dune complex. A large dune complex is called a dune field, while broad, flat regions covered with wind-swept sand or dunes, with little or no vegetation, are called ergs or sand seas. Dunes occur in different shapes and sizes, but most kinds of dunes are longer on the stoss (upflow) side, where the sand is pushed up the dune, and have a shorter slip face in the lee side. The valley or trough between dunes is called a dune slack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg/330px-Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune","wikidata":"Q25391"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg/500px-Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg/500px-Clinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Clinton Folger, mail carrier for Nantucket, towed his car to the state highway for driving to Siasconset, in observance of an early 20th-century ban on automobiles on town roads.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClinton_Folgers_%22Horsemobile%22.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg/500px-Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg/500px-Hsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1870s street scene on Nantucket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHsl-Nantucket01-horses_and_people_in_street-closeup.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg/500px-The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg/1280px-The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg/500px-The_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_%28NYPL_b12610613-422499%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The town on Nantucket Island, when it was still called Sherburne, in 1775","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_town_of_Sherburne_in_the_island_of_Nantucket_(NYPL_b12610613-422499).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Sum04-118.jpg/500px-Sum04-118.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Sum04-118.jpg/500px-Sum04-118.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The cobblestone Main Street in historic downtown Nantucket","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASum04-118.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg/500px-Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg/1280px-Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg/500px-Nantucket_NASA_2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"NASA satellite image of Nantucket Island","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANantucket_NASA_2002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Nantucket_Town_%26_County_Building.jpg/500px-Nantucket_Town_%26_County_Building.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Nantucket_Town_%26_County_Building.jpg/1280px-Nantucket_Town_%26_County_Building.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedi